  "question": {
    "text": "Species like <math><msup><msub><mi>SbCl</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>-</mo></msup><mtext>,</mtext><mtext>&nbsp;</mtext><msubsup><mi>SnCl</mi><mn>6</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mtext>&nbsp;</mtext><msup><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>+</mo></msup></math> and <math><msubsup><mi>IO</mi><mn>6</mn><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math> has hybridization as <math><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The value of <math><mtext>“x”</mtext></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3.00",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Finding the number of hybridized orbitals (by using the formula) in the central atom to find the hybridization:<br /><br /><math><mrow><mtext>H</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>V</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mtext>M</mtext> <mo>-</mo> <mtext>C</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mtext>A</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><msub><mi>SbCl</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>⇒</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> <math> <mrow> <msubsup> <mtext></mtext></msubsup></mrow></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><msub><mi>SnCl</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>⇒</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>⇒</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><msub><mi>IO</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>⇒</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>(</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p>",
